    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #43979\n\nWhen a Qwen-VL model request carries at least one real image AND literal `<image>` text in any message (e.g., from a GitHub issue/PR page replayed as a tool result), the processor incorrectly counts the user text as an image placeholder, causing:\n\n```\nMismatch: More 'IMAGE' tokens found than corresponding data provided.\n```\n\nThis is a permanent conversation-wedging bug in agent workloads.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`QwenVLImageProcessor.image_token_regex` matched both:\n1. The native chat-template tokens: `<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>`\n2. The legacy `/generate` sentinel: `<image>`\n\nThe chat template **only** emits the native sequence, so any bare `<image>` in rendered chat prompts is user text. But the combined regex made `get_combined_regex()` (used for prompt splitting/counting) treat both as real placeholders.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `python/sglang/srt/multimodal/processors/qwen_vl.py`\n\n1. **Cleaned `image_token_regex`** — removed `|<image>` alternative. The regex now only matches native chat-template tokens. This fixes the chat path: user text `<image>` is no longer counted as a placeholder.\n\n2. **Preserved legacy `/generate` path** — added a fallback in `_normalize_prompt_for_fast_path()` that normalizes `<image>` to native tokens when the prompt contains no native tokens (i.e., raw `/generate` prompts still work).\n\n## Testing\n\nVerified with a standalone regex test:\n\n| Scenario | Old regex | New regex | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Chat template: 1 native + 1 user `<image>` | count=2 (buggy) | count=1 (correct) | Bug fixed |\n| Legacy `/generate`: 2 `<image>` only | count=2 | count=2 | Still works (fallback) |\n| Chat template: 1 native, no user `<image>` | count=1 | count=1 | Unchanged |\n\nNo GPU needed — this is a pure regex fix with zero behavior change for correct inputs.\n\n---\n\nSigned-off-by: yancy <yancy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38557231040](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557231040)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557230691](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557230691)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557230901](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557230901)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
