    },
    {
      "body": "Noticed all FAIL checks are **infrastructure / pre-run gate** (`pr-gate`, `call-gate`, `Check PR title`, `check-changes`, `pr-test-*-finish`) — no lint or actual test failures on your changes. The `pr-gate` jobs fire when the PR is missing the `run-ci` label (repo-level triage workflow), `Check PR title` enforces the `[Area]: description` convention, and the `pr-test-*-finish` jobs are downstream aggregators that fail whenever upstream gates fail. Close+reopen to kick a fresh run — if you'd like full CI, a maintainer will need to add `run-ci`.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-14T11:31:30Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44149#issuecomment-6167344983",
      "id": 6167344983,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-14T11:31:30Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Asthenia0412"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing this along with all other open PRs from this account, and blocking the account from sgl-project.\n\nOver two days it opened 37 PRs, none merged: near-duplicates of the same change (four for `pp_proxy_tensors` alone), resubmissions of PRs closed the day before, test PRs, and runtime changes with no test, repro, or numbers.\n\nEvery PR here costs maintainer review time and CI. Accounts that flood the queue with unverified PRs will be closed and blocked the same way.",
